# Runtime performance (WEWIN)

Soft-nav / click TTFB is critical: aim for **tens of ms** when warm. Hundreds of ms of server work on every click is a regression.

## Soft navigation & shells
- Catalog/list chrome (`/tests`, `/learn`, …): prefer **static/ISR** (`export const revalidate = …`). See `src/app/tests/page.tsx`.
- **`SiteShell`**: client-hydrate session/ranking (`session-me`, `ranking-me`) — do **not** call `cookies()` / Prisma / auth / ranking in shared layout/shell on every soft nav.
- Defer heavy data to the **page that needs it**, not shared layout. Keep RSC payloads slim.

## Cache & data
- Semi-static data (catalog, ranking): `unstable_cache` and/or HTTP `Cache-Control` (`s-maxage`, `stale-while-revalidate`). See ranking route + `test-store`.
- Prisma: **lean `select`**, proper indexes (e.g. Attempt `userId`/`startedAt`), no N+1, no fat list payloads for admin/student lists.
- Neon Free cold starts exist — still minimize DB hits so the **warm** path stays fast; no uncached Prisma on hot nav paths.

## Media
- Serve audio/images via **R2/CDN URLs** (`src/lib/media/url.ts`), not Vercel deploy bloat or blocking nav fetches.

## When adding features
1. Ask: does this add **per-click** RSC / DB / auth work on soft nav?
2. Prefer cache, client TTL state, or deferred fetch over blocking server render in layout/shell.
3. Do **not** weaken correctness or security for speed; never hardcode secrets.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — DB/auth in layout on every soft nav
export default async function Layout({ children }) {
  const session = await getSession(); // cookies + Prisma
  const rank = await db.ranking.findMany();
  return <Shell user={session} rank={rank}>{children}</Shell>;
}

// ✅ GOOD — ISR page + client-hydrated shell (SiteShell pattern)
export const revalidate = 300;
export default async function Page() {
  return <SiteShell active="tests">{/* lean page data only */}</SiteShell>;
}
```
